    "narrative": "The offensive ceiling for LawDog today is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of the day at 74.61. His favorable matchup against Zack Littell, combined with a significant 13% boost from dynamic platoon advantages and a 10% park factor, makes him our premier start. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** (70.13) offers high-leverage potential; despite being slotted in the #8 hole, he benefits from an elite 19% SP skill boost against Rhett Lowder and a robust 14% park advantage, making him a high-efficiency play in our 5x5 structure. **Gavin Sheets** (63.91) and **JJ Bleday** (63.48) also represent strong value, as both exploit poor SP expected ERAs to maximize our run production potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Luis Arraez** (52.45), who narrowly missed the cut. While his primary upside is his elite ability to anchor the batting average category, the optimizer favored the higher cumulative scoring potential of **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho**. The latter\u2019s 10% platoon boost against Davis Martin provided just enough cushion to keep **Daulton Varsho** in the lineup over the marginal score associated with the tough matchup against Bryan Woo. We remain cautious regarding **Cal Raleigh**, whose score of 53.42 is suppressed by a difficult encounter with Logan Webb; he remains a start, but his performance will be closely monitored given the elite pedigree of the opposing arm.\n\nWe enter today with \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, which introduces non-trivial volatility for **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. While **Masyn Winn** benefits from a slow pitcher delivery profile that historically inflates our stolen base opportunities, any last-minute defensive substitutions or order shifts could degrade these projections. **Bryce Harper** maintains a solid 60.59 despite facing a quality arm in Sean Manaea, but he remains a high-risk, high-reward anchor for the lineup. With SB being our most precious commodity, we are prioritizing the volume provided by **Lawrence Butler** and **Masyn Winn** to stay competitive in an otherwise tight rotation.",
